:- module(tc, [foo/1, bar/1]).
:- chr_constraint foo(any), bar(int).
% X has two head sources: foo's `any` position and bar's `int`
% position. The concrete source wins regardless of head order (the
% `any` position binds nothing), so the body unification with a
% string literal is a type error. Companion test
% typecheck_any_order_solid_first pins the swapped head order.
bad @ foo(X), bar(X) <=> X = "oops".
